findings.body:
**A peer's slug renames use up `MAX_PEER_DECISIONS`, and that turns off the check against the peer.**

<https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/23b734cfe919ac1787e46991ed48570db631ef3f/src/core/adr-number.service.ts#L239-L251>

**Why renames count.** `peerDecisions` lists a peer through `addedAdrPaths`, which runs with `--no-renames --diff-filter=A`. So a slug-only rename of a target decision (`0005-a.md` -> `0005-b.md`) lists as an add of `0005-b.md`. `readPeer` then counts it against the cap of three (`if (theirs.size <= MAX_PEER_DECISIONS) return theirs;`).

**Why that's wrong.** ADR 0146 justifies the cap with "a competing branch that adds more than three **decisions**" (L67-69). It defines a slug rename as "that decision under a new name" (L18-20), and its Ceilings section does not accept renames counting toward the cap. A slug rename's number is already on the target, so it cannot squat anything.

**Trigger.**
1. Session P slug-renames three target ADRs and adds `0150-x.md`.
2. P's gate passes and its PR opens at a pinned sha.
3. Session Q adds `0150-y.md` and gates.
4. `readPeer` reads P and gets 4 entries, so P is `{ skipped }`. Q's stage passes with only a `not checked against pup/P` note.
5. Both PRs land, and the target holds two decisions numbered 0150. That is the #224/#237 incident this stage exists to stop.

Nothing else refuses Q:
- P was gated before Q committed.
- A re-gate only runs on the operator's `pup fix`.
- `onTarget` only catches the clash after P lands.

A squash-merged PR that has not been `pup land`ed inflates the count the same way.

**Fix.** Count only the numbers the target does not hold. Pass `onTarget` (computed at L337, before the peer loop) into `readPeer`, and keep returning the full map so the slug-rename-vs-slug-rename check (L383-390) keeps its data:

```ts
function readPeer(
  repoPath: string,
  targetSha: string,
  peer: Competitor,
  branch: string,
  onTarget: Set<number>,
): Map<string, number> | { skipped: string } | { unreadPr: string } {
  const theirs = peer.rev === undefined ? 'absent' : peerDecisions(repoPath, targetSha, peer.rev);
  if (theirs instanceof Map) {
    const fresh = [...theirs.values()].filter((number) => !onTarget.has(number)).length;
    if (fresh <= MAX_PEER_DECISIONS) return theirs;
    return {
      skipped: `it adds ${fresh} decisions, more than the ${MAX_PEER_DECISIONS} a session branch is checked for`,
    };
  }
```

Pass `onTarget` at the call site (L353). Also update the ADR's "adds more than three decisions" line and the `MAX_PEER_DECISIONS` JSDoc to say that numbers already on the target don't count.
